msgstr "埃及電子發票的法律框架"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/egypt.rst:14
msgid ""
"In Egypt, businesses must comply with electronic invoicing regulations "
"established by the `Egyptian Tax Authority (ETA) "
"<https://www.eta.gov.eg/sites/default/files/2023-03/digital-service-guide-"
"english.pdf>`_ as part of the country’s tax `digitalization "
"<https://invoicing.eta.gov.eg/content>`_ initiative. The system requires "
"taxpayers within the mandated phases to electronically issue and submit "
"invoices, credit notes, and debit notes through the ETA platform, using the "
"prescribed JSON structure and validation requirements. Documents submitted "
"to the ETA are validated and assigned a unique UUID to ensure traceability "
"and compliance. Depending on the taxpayer category and transaction type, "
"businesses are required to use digital signatures and standardized product "
"coding systems such as EGS or GS1 codes. The scope of mandatory adoption "
"continues to expand as Egypt advances its tax compliance and digital "
"transformation objectives."
msgstr ""
"在埃及，企業必須遵守由 `埃及稅務局（ETA） <https://www.eta.gov.eg/sites/"
"default/files/2023-03/digital-service-guide-english.pdf>`_ 制定的電子發票法規"
"，這是該國稅務 `數碼化 <https://invoicing.eta.gov.eg/content>`_ 倡議的一部分"
"。該制度要求屬於強制階段的納稅人，使用指定的 JSON 結構及驗證要求，透過 ETA 平"
"台以電子方式開立及提交發票、貸項通知單及借項通知單。提交至 ETA 的文件會經過驗"
"證並獲分配唯一的 UUID，以確保可追溯性及合規性。視乎納稅人類別及交易類型，企業"
"須使用數碼簽署及標準化產品編碼系統（例如 EGS 或 GS1 編碼）。隨著埃及不斷推進"
"稅務合規及數碼轉型目標，強制採用的範圍亦持續擴大。"

