#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:5
msgid "Odoo electronic invoicing in Saudi Arabia"
msgstr "沙特阿拉伯的 Odoo 電子發票"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:7
msgid ""
"Odoo Invoicing is your trusted partner for safe, efficient, and legally "
"compliant e-invoicing solutions tailored to meet Saudi Arabia’s regulatory "
"standards and compatible with the requirements set forth by the Zakat, Tax "
"and Customs Authority."
msgstr ""
"Odoo 發票管理是您值得信賴的合作夥伴，提供安全、高效且符合法規的電子發票解決方"
"案，專為滿足沙特阿拉伯的監管標準而設，並符合天課、稅務及海關總局（ZATCA）的規"
"定。"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:12
msgid "Legal framework for e-invoicing in Saudi Arabia"
msgstr "沙特阿拉伯電子發票的法律框架"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:14
msgid ""
"In Saudi Arabia, businesses must comply with `electronic invoicing "
"regulations "
"<https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Introduction/LawsAndRegulations/Documents/20230519_E-"
"Invoicing%20Implementation%20Resolution%20English.pdf>`_ established by the "
"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA) under the E-Invoicing Regulations "
"and their associated implementation resolutions. `The e-invoicing framework "
"<https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Introduction/Pages/What-is-e-"
"invoicing.aspx>`_ applies to taxpayers subject to VAT in the Kingdom and is "
"implemented in two phases. Phase 1 (Generation Phase) requires businesses to"
" generate and store electronic invoices and notes in a compliant electronic "
"format, including mandatory fields and QR codes. Phase 2 (Integration Phase)"
" introduces integration with ZATCA’s platform for invoice clearance and "
"reporting through APIs. Businesses must issue tax invoices for B2B "
"transactions and simplified tax invoices for B2C transactions in accordance "
"with ZATCA’s technical and procedural requirements. The framework also "
"requires the issuance of electronic credit and debit notes linked to the "
"original invoice, while ensuring invoice authenticity, integrity, and "
"traceability through structured XML formats and cryptographic controls."
msgstr ""
"在沙特阿拉伯，企業必須遵守由天課、稅務及海關總局（ZATCA）根據《電子發票法規》"
"及其相關實施決議制定的 `電子發票法規 <https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/"
"Introduction/LawsAndRegulations/Documents/20230519_E-"
"Invoicing%20Implementation%20Resolution%20English.pdf>`_ 。 `電子發票框架 "
"<https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Introduction/Pages/What-is-e-"
"invoicing.aspx>`_ 適用於該王國境內須繳納增值稅的納稅人，並分兩個階段實施。第"
"一階段（生成階段）要求企業以合規的電子格式生成並儲存電子發票及票據，當中須包"
"含必填欄位及二維碼。第二階段（整合階段）則引入與 ZATCA 平台的整合，透過 API "
"進行發票清關及申報。企業必須根據 ZATCA 的技術及程序要求，為 B2B 交易開具稅務"
"發票，以及為 B2C 交易開具簡化稅務發票。該框架亦要求開具與原始發票關聯的電子貸"
"項及借項通知單，同時透過結構化 XML 格式及加密控制措施確保發票的真實性、完整性"
"及可追溯性。"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/customer_invoices/electronic_invoicing/saudi_arabia.rst:29
msgid "Compliance with Saudi Arabia’s e-invoicing regulations"
msgstr "遵守沙特阿拉伯的電子發票法規"

