#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/germany.rst:128
msgid ""
"Set the :guilabel:`Taxable Supply Date` on invoices to reflect the actual "
"delivery date for goods or services provided before invoice creation (e.g., "
"service delivered in May, invoice created in June). Completing this field "
"automatically aligns the invoice's accounting date, ensuring that the "
"journal entry and the associated VAT are recognized in the correct period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/germany.rst:134
msgid ""
"If the previous period is closed and locked (via :ref:`Lock dates "
"<accounting/tax-returns/lock-date>`), postings for that period are not "
"allowed. Consequently, the journal entry will automatically be posted in the"
" current open period."
msgstr ""
"如果上一個會計期間已關閉並鎖定（透過 :ref:`鎖定日期 <accounting/tax-returns/"
"lock-date>`），則不允許在該期間過賬。因此，日記賬分錄會自動過賬至目前開放的會"
"計期間。"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/germany.rst:139
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`Taxable Supply Date field` is intended for accounting "
"purposes and is not displayed on printed reports. When using the "
":guilabel:`DIN 5008` layout, ensure the :guilabel:`Delivery Date` field is "
"filled to display the date on the generated PDF invoice."
